  "id": "DrugBank_DB09013 - MONDO_5338",
  "verbalization": "Befunolol is associated with Open-angle Glaucoma through a chain of indications that involve ocular hypertension, a condition that is a known risk factor for the development of open-angle glaucoma. The evidence suggests that Befunolol may exert a role in the pathogenesis of open-angle glaucoma through its effects on ocular hypertension, which in turn could influence intraocular pressure and contribute to the progression of the disease. The presence of multiple pathways linking Befunolol to ocular hypertension, and subsequently to open-angle glaucoma, indicates a potential mechanism involving the modulation of ocular physiology. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of ocular hypertension as a mediator in the relationship between Befunolol and open-angle glaucoma, suggesting that Befunolol may influence ocular homeostasis in a way that could contribute to the development of this condition.",
